      "status": "ok",
      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence fully explains how the paper's Ngram language models are used to make predictions on humorous statements: models are trained on two corpora (funny @midnight tweets and a news corpus), each tweet is assigned a probability by each model, and funnier tweets are those with higher probability under the funny-tweet model and lower probability under the news model, allowing relative ranking. Bigrams and trigrams are used as features with KenLM and modified Kneser-Ney smoothing. The paper also outlines planned deep learning extensions (CNNs, LSTMs), though deep learning is presented as future work rather than the actual prediction method, which the evidence supports."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 3582.681500003673
